     "page": 1,
     "text": "Johnson Inc Clinic\nRe: Eric Moran (DOB 02/21/2007)\n\nDear Sir or Madam,\n\nI am writing to provide medical information on my patient, Eric Moran, who has been under my care since he was diagnosed with systemic Lupus in December 2023. As requested, will detail his medical history, current condition, and compliance with treatment.\n\nOn June 01, 2025, Eric was seen for his Lupus management. His blood pressure was 122/68, and he weighed 113 pounds. His overall condition appeared stable with no new organ involvement, and he was managing well with his current medication regimen of mycophenolate 500 mg and hydroxychloroquine 200 mg.\n\nThroughout his visits, Eric has generally done well with his condition being well-controlled. However, it has come to my attention that Eric has been non-compliant with his medication regimen and missed two follow-up appointments. This lack of adherence may have implications for his long-term health and the management of his Lupus.\n\nEric is also a cigar smoker, with a frequency of about 8 cigars per year, a habit he has maintained since June 2009. Additionally, he consumes approximately 12 alcoholic drinks per week. \n\nHis mother has a history of COPD, diagnosed at the age of G9, although she is still living.\n\nHis recent visit on January 11, 2025, showed a blood pressure of 109/78 and a weight of 120 pounds. His condition remained stable, and he continued on his medications.\n\nI hope this information is helpful. Please let me know if you require any additional details.\n\nSincere\n"
    }
